#4. READ INTENSIVE APPLICATION KO KAISE SCALE KAREIN?   - READ REPLICAS
============================================================================

Maan lo application par read requests bahut zyada hain aur write requests comparatively kam hain.

Example (E-commerce):

    Product View          → Very Frequent (90% READ)
    Product Create/Update → Relatively Less Frequent (10% WRITE)

Initially system comfortably handle kar raha hota hai.

                Application
                     |
         +-----------+-----------+
         |                       |
       READ                    WRITE
         |                       |
         +-----------+-----------+
                     |
                     v
                 Single DB

Ab application popular ho gayi aur traffic significantly increase ho gaya.

Assume karo:

    100,000 requests/sec

        90,000 → READ
        10,000 → WRITE


Ab 90,000 read requests bhi isi single database ko hit karengi,
to database ke CPU aur memory par significant load aa sakta hai,
aur application ka configured DB connection pool bhi saturate ho sakta hai.

Isse database bottleneck ban sakta hai:

    Higher DB Load
         ↓
    Higher Query Latency
         ↓
    Lower Application Throughput


----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## QUESTION: KYA READ REQUESTS KO HANDLE KARNE KE LIYE CACHE KA USE KIYA JA SAKTA HAI?
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Haan.

Agar same data baar-baar request ho raha hai, to hum frequently accessed
data ko Redis jaise cache mein store karke repeated database reads ko reduce
kar sakte hain.

Lekin caching har read workload ko completely solve nahi karti.

Cache tab zyada useful hota hai jab:

- Same data repeatedly request ho raha ho.
- Data relatively frequently change na ho. Agar data bahut frequently change
  ho raha hoga, to baar-baar shared cache (redis) invalidate karna padta hai, jo ek alag
  overhead hai. Agar application local cache bhi maintain kar raha ho, to
  different instances ke local cache ko invalidate karna difficult ho sakta hai
  aur overhead badh sakta hai.

Agar requests mostly unique data ke liye hain, even though hum application aur database 
ke beech caching layer use kar rahe hain, tab bhi cache misses zyada ho sakte hain aur 
database ko still significant read traffic handle karna pad sakta hai.

Isliye large read-intensive applications mein hum application aur database ke beech 
cache layer use kar sakte hain, taaki frequently accessed data cache se serve ho.
Lekin agar cache ke baad bhi database par high read load hai, to database side par 
read scaling ki zarurat pad sakti hai.

Database read scaling ke liye hum Read Replicas introduce kar sakte hain.


