4. DIRECTORY / LOOKUP-BASED SHARDING
--------------------------------------
Directory / Lookup-Based Sharding mein Application (ya dedicated Shard Routing Layer i.e Database Proxy / Routing Service)
ek separate mapping / lookup table maintain karti hai. Is mapping ke basis par decide kiya jaata hai ki particular data
kis Shard mein store hoga aur future mein usi data ke UPDATE / DELETE requests ko kis Shard par route kiya jaayega.


## BENIFITS :
----------------

1: FLEXIBILITY
----------------

Directory / Lookup-Based Sharding ka biggest benefit flexibility hai.

Shard 1 → Heavy Load
Shard 2 → Medium Load
Shard 3 → Low Load

Agar new User create ho raha hai, Shard Routing Layer usse suitable Shard, jaise Shard 3, par store kar sakti hai.

Uske baad Directory mein mapping store hoti hai:

user_id = 101 → Shard 3

Future Update/Delete requests mein:

user_id = 101
        ↓
Directory Lookup
        ↓
Shard 3

Yaani Directory mapping ke through future requests consistently usi Shard par route hoti hain jahan User ka data stored hai.


2: FLEXIBLE REBALANCING 
-------------------------

Agar kisi particular data ke liye bahut zyada write requests aa rahi hain aur woh data kisi particular Shard par stored hai, 
to us Shard par disproportionate load aa sakta hai aur woh Hot Shard ban sakta hai.
Aise case mein heavily accessed data ko comparatively underutilized Shard par migrate kiya ja sakta hai.
Migration ke baad Lookup / Directory Mapping ko update kar diya jaata hai, taaki future requests naye Shard par route ho sakein.

Is approach ka advantage ye hai ki routing kisi fixed Range ya Hash Formula
par directly dependent nahi hoti.

Isliye selected keys/data ko independently migrate karke unki mapping update
ki ja sakti hai.



## LIMITATIONS :
----------------

Correct Shard identify karne ke liye Application ya dedicated
Shard Routing Layer (for example, Database Proxy / Routing Service) ko
pehle Lookup / Directory Mapping check karni pad sakti hai.

Isse:

- Additional Network Call ho sakti hai.
- Overall Request Latency increase ho sakti hai.
- Lookup / Directory Layer khud Single Point of Failure (SPOF) ban sakti hai.


## SINGLE POINT OF FAILURE KA RISK
-----------------------------------

Agar Lookup / Directory Service single instance mein running hai aur
woh unavailable ho jaati hai, to Application correct Shard identify
nahi kar paayegi.

Isliye Production Systems mein Lookup / Directory Layer ko bhi
Highly Available banana padta hai.

Iske liye commonly Multiple Replicated Instances maintain ki jaati hain.



