## QUESTION: SHARDING KE BAAD READ REPLICAS KAISE WORK KARTI HAIN?
--------------------------------------------------------------------

Non-Sharded Read Scaled Architecture mein:

Writes → Primary Database
Reads → Read Replicas

Read Replicas Primary Database se data replicate karti hain.

Lekin Sharding ke baad data multiple Shards mein distributed hota hai.

Har Shard total dataset ka sirf ek subset store karta hai aur
apne assigned data ke Write Traffic ko handle karta hai.


## QUESTION : AGAR WRITE TRAFFIC MULTIPLE SHARDS KE ACROSS DISTRIBUTE HO CHUKA HAI, TO HAR SHARD KE READ TRAFFIC KO KAISE SCALE KIYA JAAYEGA?
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Sharding ke baad har Shard apne assigned subset of data ke Writes
handle karta hai aur apne Read Traffic ko scale karne ke liye
multiple Read Replicas maintain kar sakta hai.

Architecture conceptually kuch aisi hogi:

                         REQUEST
                            |
                            v
                      Application
                            |
                            v
                    Shard Routing Layer
                            |
              +-------------+-------------+
              |                           |
              v                           v
         Logical Shard 1             Logical Shard 2
              |                           |
              v                           v
          Primary DB                  Primary DB
           /       \                   /       \
          v         v                 v         v
      Replica 1   Replica 2       Replica 1   Replica 2


## WRITE REQUEST FLOW
------------------------

Jab bhi Write Request aati hai, Application request se Shard Key ki value identify karti hai.
Us Shard Key par Shard Routing Logic apply karke pehle correct Shard identify kiya jaata hai.
Uske baad Write Request directly us Shard ke Primary Database par execute hoti hai.

Write successfully execute hone ke baad, Shard 2 ka Primary Database
apne corresponding Read Replicas ko data replicate karta hai.


## READ REQUEST FLOW
----------------------

Jab bhi Read Request aati hai, Application request se Shard Key ki value identify karti hai.
Us Shard Key par Shard Routing Logic apply karke pehle correct Shard identify kiya jaata hai.
Uske baad Application us particular Shard ke available Read Replicas mein se
kisi ek Replica ko select karti hai.

Selected Read Replica se data fetch karke Application response return kar deti hai.


