## QUESTION: DATABASE DATA KO STORE KAISE KARTA HAI?
-------------------------------------------------------
Database data ko individual rows ke form mein directly disk par 
store nahi karta hai.Instead, database table ke rows ko fixed-size
chunks, called Pages (ya Blocks), mein organize aur store karta hai.

Database Pages eventually physical disk ke data blocks mein store hote hain.
Physical disk par bahut saare data blocks hote hain, aur har block ka fixed size hota hai.

Ek physical data block mein ek ya ek se zyada database pages store ho sakte hain, 
depending on their respective sizes.

Database ke perspective se DBMS database pages ko manage karta hai, jabki physical disk 
level par actual storage blocks ko OS/filesystem/storage layer manage karti hai.

DBMS internally database pages aur physical disk blocks ke beech mapping maintain karta hai,
taaki required database page ko **locate kiya ja sake**.

Ek data page generally ek specific table ke subset of rows contain krta hai, 
Ek table ke saare rows ko store karne ke liye multiple database pages
required ho sakte hain.

Database page ka size DBMS/storage engine ke according different ho sakta hai,
jaise 4 KB, 8 KB, ya 16 KB.

DBMS in database pages ko create aur manage karta hai.


## STRUCTURE OF DATA PAGE
---------------------------

┌──────────────────────────────────┐
│         HEADER                   │
│  Page No. | Free Space | Checksum│ 
├──────────────────────────────────┤
│      DATA RECORDS                │
│                                  │
│  Row 1 → (1, Anand, 25)          │ ← Table ki actual Row 1
│  Row 2 → (2, Rahul, 26)          │ ← Table ki actual Row 2
│  Row 3 → (3, Amit, 24)           │ ← Table ki actual Row 3
│                                  │
├──────────────────────────────────┤
│         OFFSET ARRAY             │
│                                  │
│  offset[0] → Pointer to Row 1    │
│  offset[1] → Pointer to Row 2    │
│  offset[2] → Pointer to Row 3    │
└──────────────────────────────────┘


Jab bhi kisi particular row ya rows par READ / INSERT / UPDATE operation perform karna hota hai, 
database ko operation perform karne ke liye relevant page/pages ko RAM mein access karna hota hai.

Agar required page already RAM ke Buffer Pool mein available hai, 
to database directly usi page par operation perform karta hai.

Agar required page Buffer Pool mein available nahi hai, to database use disk
se RAM mein load karta hai aur phir required operation perform karta hai.

RAM ka woh area jahan database pages temporarily store hote hain, Buffer Pool kehlata hai.


