## QUESTION: DATABASE INDEXING KYA HAI AND KYUN REQUIRED HAI ?
-----------------------------------------------------------------

Indexing ek technique hai jisse database queries ko faster banaya jata hai.

Generally, jis column ka use queries mein frequently hota hai, hum us column par index define kar dete hain.
Index ki help se database easily identify kar sakta hai ki required row/rows kis database page mein stored hai, 
jisse un rows ko quickly locate kiya ja sakta hai.

Without Indexing, database ke paas generally directly yeh information nahi hoti ki required row/rows
kis data page mein stored hain. Isliye unhe dhoondhne ke liye database ko table se associated  multiple 
data pages ko scan karna pad sakta hai. Large table ke case mein database ko bahut saare database pages 
check karne pad sakte hain. Is process ko broadly Full Table Scan kaha jata hai.

Index implement karne ke liye databases commonly B+ Tree use karte hain.


## QUESTION : B+ TREE KYA HOTA HAI ?
---------------------------------------

B+ Tree ek self-balancing, tree-based data structure hai.

M-order B+ Tree mein ek node mein maximum M child pointers aur M−1 keys ho sakti hain.

For example:

Order 3 → maximum 3 children and 2 keys

3-order B+ Tree ke ek internal node ka structure:

              ┌──────────┬──────────┬──────────┬──────────┬──────────┐
              │ Pointer 1│   Key 1  │ Pointer 2│   Key 2  │ Pointer 3│
              └────┬─────┴──────────┴────┬─────┴──────────┴────┬─────┘
                   │                     │                     │
                   ▼                     ▼                     ▼
             Child Node 1          Child Node 2          Child Node 3
             Values < Key 1      Key 1 <= Values < Key 2    Values >= Key 2


B+ Tree construct karne ke liye jin input values ka use kiya jata hai, 
woh eventually leaf nodes mein zaroor present hoti hain.

Internal nodes mein un input values (jinhe keys kehte hain) ki copies exist kar sakti 
hain, lekin actual input values leaf nodes mein hi maintained hoti hain.

Internal/non-leaf nodes ki keys mainly separator keys ke roop mein kaam karti hain,
jisse database appropriate child aur eventually relevant leaf node tak pahunch sake.

B+ Tree mein keys sorted order mein maintained hoti hain.

B+ Tree mein sabhi leaf nodes same level par hoti hain, aur leaf nodes generally sequentially
interconnected hoti hain via linked list.


## QUESTION : DBMS INDEXES KAISE MAINTAIN KARTA HAI ?
------------------------------------------------------

DBMS indexed column ki values ke basis par B+ Tree construct karta hai.

B+ Tree mein indexed column ki values leaf nodes mein (as a key) sorted order mein stored hoti hain, 
aur us key ke corresponding row ko locate karne wala reference bhi maintained hota hai.

Lookup ke time internal/non-leaf nodes ki keys navigation purpose ke liye use hoti hain,
jisse database appropriate leaf node tak pahunch sake.

Exactly kya reference stored hota hai — jaise database page ka reference, row ka reference, ya actual row —
ye DBMS, storage engine aur index type (clustered vs non-clustered) par depend karta hai.

Since B+ tree mai leaf nodes sequentially interconnected hoti hain via linked list. is wajah se database ko
range scans (jaise SELECT * FROM table WHERE id BETWEEN 10 AND 50) ko efficiently perform karne deti hai
Ek baar leaf par pahunch gaye, toh bas next pointer follow karte raho.



QUESTION: AGAR HUMEIN KOI PARTICULAR ROW RETRIEVE KARNI HO, TO DATABASE KO KAISE PATA CHALTA HAI KI WO ROW KIS PAGE MEIN STORED HAI?
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Example:

SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = 5;

### WITHOUT INDEX
-------------------

Agar id column par koi index nahi hai, to database ke paas directly yeh 
information nahi hoti ki id = 5 wali row kis data page mein stored hai.

Isliye database ko required row dhoondhne ke liye us table se associated
data pages ko potentially scan karna pad sakta hai.

Large table ke case mein database ko bahut saare pages check karne pad sakte hain. 
Is process ko broadly Full Table Scan kaha jata hai.


### WITH INDEX
-----------------
Relational databases commonly B-Tree/B+ Tree type data structure ko index ke implementation ke liye use karte hain.


